OL,3,GNEWSAHistory buffs create 'Bayeux
OL,4,ATapestry' of village
OL,5,
OL,6,FA village is hoping to interest more
OL,7,Fpeople in local history with the
OL,8,Fcreation of its own "Bayeux Tapestry".
OL,10,FInspired by the 70-metre long artwork
OL,11,Fwhich is currently on loan to the
OL,12,FBritish Museum, history buffs in
OL,13,FHockham, Norfolk, commissioned their
OL,14,Fown printed cloth version which starts
OL,15,Fwith the 1066 Norman Conquest and the
OL,16,Fmention of their village in the
OL,17,FDomesday Book of 1086.
OL,19,FThe 5m (16ft)-long cloth details other
OL,20,Fsignificant events such as the granting
OL,21,Fof its market charter and soldiers
OL,22,Freturning from World War One.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
